        "comments": "The assembly of Phycis blennoides (fPhyBle1) is based on 35X ONT data and 62X Arima Hi-C data generated as part of the ATLASea programme (https://www.atlasea.fr). The assembly process included the following steps: initial ONT assembly generation with Hifiasm, removal of contaminant sequences using Context, removal of haplotypic duplications using purge_dups, and Hi-C-based scaffolding with YaHS. No contigs were found to be contaminants (bacterial, archaeal, or viral). Additionally, 90 regions totaling 16.007 Mb (with the largest being 2.067 Mb) were identified as haplotypic duplications and removed. Mitochondrial genome was assembled using ptGAUL. Finally, the primary assembly was analyzed and manually improved using Pretext. During manual curation, 4 haplotypic regions and 2 contaminant sequences were removed, totaling 0.664Mb and 0.42Mb, respectively (with the largest being 0.447Mb and 0.368Mb). Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by Hi-C data were named in order of size.",
